act sets to the wanderer line ensembles constructed in [7]. line Airy we Airy","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":486.04297559556653,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":94.66666666666667,"r":517.0,"t":575.0},"charspan":[0,821],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"We consider family of Pfaffian Schur processes whose first coordinate marginal relates to the half space geometric last passage percolation. We show that the ensembles corresponding to the Pfaffian Schur processes with geometric weights converge uniformly over compact sets to the line ensemble_ By detailed asymptotic analysis of the kernels; can verify the conditions for the finite dimensional weak convergence introduced in [7]. By utilizing the tightness criteria of the line ensembles established in [8] , we can further improve the finite dimensional convergence to the uniform convergence over compact sets. Moreover, using the same methodology we also show that sequences of spiked Pfaffian Schur processes converge uniformly over compact sets to the wanderer line ensembles constructed in [7]. line Airy we Airy"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"Contents","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":455.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.0,"r":136.33333333333334,"t":469.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,8],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Contents"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"1 Introduction and main results","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":203.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.33333333333333,"r":310.0,"t":220.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,31],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"1 Introduction and main results"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"half-space were extensively studied. For example; [1] studied the fluctuations of last passage percolation with exponential weights in half-quadrant within the framework of Pfaflian Schur processes; [17] shows the fluctuations of a one-dimensional polynuclear growth model in a half-space; the gamma polymer in a half space was also considered [13] . a amount of half-space models; the fluctuations follow the GUE Widom distribution in the bulk. It is interesting to further investigate if these models converges to the Airy line ensemble. For large Tracy","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":121.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":542.3333333333334,"t":195.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,555],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/7","text":"half-space were extensively studied. For example; [1] studied the fluctuations of last passage percolation with exponential weights in half-quadrant within the framework of Pfaflian Schur processes; [17] shows the fluctuations of a one-dimensional polynuclear growth model in a half-space; the gamma polymer in a half space was also considered [13] . a amount of half-space models; the fluctuations follow the GUE Widom distribution in the bulk. It is interesting to further investigate if these models converges to the Airy line ensemble. For large Tracy"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The line ensemble is a random sequence of continuous functions that arises as a scaling limit in random matrix theory and various models within the KPZ universality class [5, 6, 15, 18] In particular , LAiry Airy","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":97.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.66666666666667,"r":541.6666666666666,"t":123.52590292133323},"charspan":[0,212],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/8","text":"The line ensemble is a random sequence of continuous functions that arises as a scaling limit in random matrix theory and various models within the KPZ universality class [5, 6, 15, 18] In particular , LAiry Airy"}],"version":"1.10.0"}